    35	- `rtx-serve` (filter jobs.serve.>) has never had a live subscriber in this snapshot; it is a demo consumer from build day.
    36	
    37	## Recent journal signals (from `journalctl -u nats` on the nodes)
    38	- 2026-08-15 20:31:54 on nats1 and nats3: `[ERR] <lan-address> … authentication error - User "route"` — something on the node1 PVE host tried the cluster-route user on the CLIENT port 4222 (the route password lives in plaintext in each node's config file, in the `routes` URLs).
    39	- 2026-08-15 20:35–20:42: stream `ESTATE > FIX2SCRATCH` with consumers `s2` and `scratch-serve` got leaders — a scratch stream created ad hoc on the production spine during some fix session; it is not in the current stream list (deleted since).
    40	- 2026-08-15 06:03: nats3 became meta leader ("Self is new JetStream cluster metadata leader") after a node event; the last meta snapshot is from 2026-08-15 20:43.
    41	- No restarts of nats.service on any node since each CT's last boot (NRestarts=0).
    42	
    43	## Backup / maintenance windows
    44	- PVE hourly `vzdump` (all guests, snapshot mode, to iscsi-fast) runs at the top of every hour. Estate rule: check cluster tasks and avoid the :00 windows before any disruptive op (a reboot during vzdump once locked a live-trading CT for 20 h).
    45	- `nats-store-monitor.timer` on node1 polls `/jsz` on all three nodes every 15 min and alerts at >80% of 15 GB; the last runs show 0%. It only checks store bytes — not version, quorum, leader, or consumer lag.
    46	- Cross-node `estate-deadman` watchdog exists (pings node1/2/3), unrelated to NATS health.
    47	
    48	## Who depends on the spine right now
    49	- CT 116 hale-support (durable `support-intake` on EVENTS; `clickup-ingest`-adjacent) — the LIVE support desk (email → tickets). NATS is a freshness path; CT116 falls back to 10-min polling if NATS is down.
    50	- CT 201 halebrain — `embed-workers`, `hale-eval-workers`/`collector`, `clickup-ingest` (HAL ingestion). Batch/async; restart-survivable by design.
    51	- Nothing else. GPU workers (`rtx`/`arm` users) are not yet wired in.

